openqmc-rs
==========

This crate is a Rust port of OpenQMC, a quasi-Monte Carlo sampling library:

    https://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/openqmc
    Copyright Contributors to the OpenQMC Project.
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The port reproduces the upstream algorithms (PCG hashing, hash-based Owen
scrambling of Sobol sequences per Burley 2020 and Ahmed 2024, rank-1 lattices
per Hickernell et al., progressive multi-jittered (0,2) sequences per Helmer et
al., and the domain-tree sampler interface) and their sample values bit-for-bit.

Bundled data (`src/data/*.bin`) are the upstream optimised blue-noise key/rank
tables (`include/oqmc/data/**`) converted verbatim to little-endian binary.
Those tables in turn derive from work by Belcour & Heitz; the Sobol direction
matrices originate from MIT-licensed code by Leonhard Gruenschloss.

A copy of the Apache License, Version 2.0 is provided in the LICENSE file
alongside this notice.
